//
// The version reaches the installer through a generated header rather than a
// string compile-definition, because the quotes around a -D string do not
// survive the trip through CMake, MSBuild and the compiler. A header has no
// quoting layers to lose, and it is checked into the build rather than
// assembled on a command line.
